  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "text": "Three animals that sleep in the craziest ways."
    },
    {
      "id": "otter1",
      "text": "First, sea otters. If one falls asleep alone, the current can carry it far out to sea."
    },
    {
      "id": "otter2",
      "text": "So they hold hands while they sleep, so nobody drifts away.",
      "sfx": [
        [
          "pop",
          2
        ],
        [
          "wrong",
          9
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "otter3",
      "text": "Some even wrap themselves in kelp, like a blanket tied to the ocean floor."
    },
    {
      "id": "otter4",
      "text": "And the babies? They just nap on mom's belly.",
      "sfx": [
        [
          "pop",
          2
        ],
        [
          "pop",
          7
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "frigate1",
      "text": "Next, the frigatebird. It can stay in the air for two whole months without landing.",
      "sfx": [
        [
          "pop",
          9
        ],
        [
          "counter",
          10
        ],
        [
          "wrong",
          14
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "frigate2",
      "text": "So it sleeps while flying, in naps that last about twelve seconds,",
      "sfx": [
        [
          "pop",
          5,
          0.1
        ],
        [
          "counter",
          9
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "frigate3",
      "text": "often with half of its brain still awake to watch where it's going.",
      "sfx": [
        [
          "pop",
          2
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "frigate4",
      "text": "Add it all up, and that's less than forty-five minutes of sleep a day.",
      "sfx": [
        [
          "pop",
          0,
          0.1
        ],
        [
          "pop",
          6
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "whale1",
      "text": "Finally, sperm whales. They sleep standing straight up, hanging just below the surface like giant tree trunks.",
      "sfx": [
        [
          "pop",
          15
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "whale2",
      "text": "The whole group goes completely still for up to fifteen minutes.",
      "sfx": [
        [
          "pop",
          9
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "whale3",
      "text": "When scientists drifted their boat right into a sleeping pod, the whales didn't even notice.",
      "sfx": [
        [
          "whoosh",
          0,
          -0.1
        ],
        [
          "pop",
          12
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "whale4",
      "text": "Until the boat bumped one, and the whole group woke up at once.",
      "sfx": [
        [
          "splash",
          3
        ],
        [
          "splash",
          9
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
